title: Hypoparathyroidism
---

# Hypoparathyroidism

- **Definition** - insufficient PTH secretion manifesting as hypocalcaemia
- **Etiology of hypoparathyroidism:**
  - <u>Iatrogenic</u> (most common):
    - Thyroidectomy - due to damage to PTH gland or to its blood supply (occurs in up to 9% in total thyroidectomy)
  - <u>Infiltrative</u>:
    - Haemochromatosis
    - Wilson's disease
  - <u>Inherited causes of hypoparathyroidism</u>:
    - Autoimmune polyendocrine syndrome type 1
    - DiGeorge syndrome
    - Autosomal dominant hypoparathyroidism (mirror immage of FHH)
- **Mx:**
  - **Principles of Mx:**
    - <u>Replacement of Ca and vitamin D</u> - oral calcium salt and vitamin D analogues 1,25(OH2)D
    - <u>Recombinant PTH</u> - SC injections are typicaly not licensed for hypoparathyroidism
